<title>USA: Blount to buy back up to $50 mln in stock.</title>
<headline>Blount to buy back up to $50 mln in stock.</headline>
<dateline>MONTGOMERY, Ala. 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Blount International Inc said on Monday its board of directors authorized the repurchase of up to $50 million of its Class A common stock.</p>
<p>&quot;Despite record sales and earnings, Blount's shares have continued to trade at a significant discount to the shares of its peers,&quot; said president and chief executive officer John Panettiere.</p>
<p>He said Blount has excess available funds with which to complete this program, while continuing to invest in its core businesses, as well as make strategic acquisitions.</p>
</text>
